<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE cygnus-ng25-2026-11-29 ascent</name><description>ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Falcon 9 Cygnus NG-25 (SLC-40) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
PRE-FLIGHT. T0 is 2026-11-29T15:47:00Z (Sun 29 Nov 10:47 a.m. ET). LL2 id d74afbc7-0de5-491c-be05-4e9c31f736ac, Go, NET 2026-11-29T15:47:00Z, minute precision, window fields both 15:47:00Z, last_updated 2026-11-26T11:44:54Z. SpaceX https://www.spacex.com/launches/ng25 prose: liftoff targeted for 10:47 a.m. ET. SOURCE CONFLICT: the same page&#x27;s header is the window 29 Nov 10:40-11:00 ET (15:40-16:00Z). Used the 15:47Z instant. Backup Mon 30 Nov 10:24 a.m. ET = 2026-11-30T15:24:00Z. Ninth flight. Landing on Landing Zone 40.
Published timeline (SpaceX ng25): Max-Q 1:08, MECO 2:13, stage sep 2:17, SES-1 2:24, fairing 2:53, boostback 2:30-3:21, entry 6:09-6:26, landing burn 7:24, LZ-40 landing 7:49, SECO-1 8:32, Cygnus XL deploys 14:35. SECO and deploy ARE published. This surrogate still ends at the family-telemetry end T+508 s, before SECO.
Loft: FALCON 9 FAMILY SURROGATE, Iridium NEXT-7 altitude and downrange vs time, laid on this flight&#x27;s azimuth. https://github.com/shahar603/Telemetry-Data/tree/master/Iridium%20NEXT%207
  That flight&#x27;s MECO was T+146 s. This flight&#x27;s MECO is T+133 s (RTLS). The loft is a family stand-in, not this timeline. FILE ENDS AT T+508 s (telemetry end).
Azimuth 46.36 deg: great-circle bearing from the LL2 SLC-40 pad to the midpoint of the far edge of NAVAREA IV 1141/26 Area B. Edge 31-57.00N 076-28.00W to 31-51.00N 076-17.00W. Midpoint 31.9000N 76.3750W. Bearing unrounded 46.364 deg, rounded to 46.36. Distance 548.3 km. https://www.sealagom.com/navarea/4/message/26132/1141-26-north-atlantic/
  Non-rotating inclination from 46.36 deg is 50.53 deg. Area A of the same notice is a near-shore box within about 49 km of the pad (one vertex is northwest of the pad) and was not used. Its downrange-edge bearing is about 52.04 deg. The 29 Nov period on the notice is 15:40-16:43Z, which starts at the SpaceX window open.
ASSUMPTION on the plane: the factsheet initial orbit is 245 x 245 km at 51.64 deg. The azimuth was taken from Area B and was not retuned to 51.64 deg or to 51.6 deg. ILLUSTRATIVE.
Velocity = backward difference of ECEF position (Earth-relative). Pad (LL2): 28.561941N -80.577357E. Elevation ASSUMED 0 m. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s.
Constant-azimuth rhumb Az=46.36 deg from pad (spherical R=6371.0088 km).
T0 used: 2026-11-29T15:47:00Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.</description>
